<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Francis II Rákóczi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1676">1676</a>–<a href="/years/1735">1735</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francis-ii">Francis II</a> Rákóczi was a Hungarian noble who led the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rakoczis-war-of-independence">Rákóczi's War of Independence</a> against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburg</a> rule from 1703 to 1711. Elected <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prince-of-transylvania">Prince of Transylvania</a> in 1704 and ruling prince of the confederated estates of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a>, he fought with French support but was defeated. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peace-of-szatmar">Peace of Szatmár</a> in 1711 ended the revolt, and he died in exile in Ottoman Rodosto.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/francis-ii-rakoczi.jpg" alt="Francis II Rákóczi" width="320" height="396" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ádám Mányoki · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:II._R%C3%A1k%C3%B3czi_Ferenc_M%C3%A1nyoki.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
